{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task is AGENT-TF-01: implement `solve(case)` that filters API calls using Toolformer-style loss filtering.\n\nKey algorithm from the candidate_artifact:\n1. For each call: `gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n2. Normalize gain by prediction tokens: `normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens`\n3. A call is accepted if: `parseable == True` AND `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n4. Return diagnostics in supplied call order\n5. Return accepted call IDs\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture:\n- threshold: 0.05\n- call0: gain = 1.48911432 - 0.30132987 = 1.18778445, normalized = 1.18778445/5 = 0.23755689, parseable=true → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.37006381 - 0.10127803 = 1.26878578, normalized = 1.26878578/5 = 0.25375716, parseable=true → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.07992348 - 0.04054692 = 1.03937656, normalized = 1.03937656/5 = 0.20787531, parseable=true → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.76582941 - 0.57732788 = 1.18850153, normalized = 1.18850153/3 = 0.39616718, parseable=true → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.70674574 - 0.40289862 = 1.30384712, normalized = 1.30384712/6 = 0.21730785, parseable=true → accepted\n- call5: gain = 1.98682122 - 0.89260518 = 1.09421604, normalized = 1.09421604/4 = 0.27355401, parseable=false → rejected\n\nSo accepted: call0, call1, call2, call3, call4\n\nThe output schema requires:\n- `accepted_call_ids`: list of strings\n- `diagnostics`: list of objects with `accepted`, `call_id`, `normalized_gain`\n\nThe candidate artifact says \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" - need to figure out rounding. It doesn't specify decimal places explicitly, but I'll round to a reasonable precision. Looking at the schema, `normalized_gain` is just `type: number`, so I could round to e.g. 4 decimal places.\n\nActually, let me not over-specify rounding - let me just use Python's round() to some reasonable number of places like 4 or leave it as is. Since it says \"rounded\", I'll round to 4 decimal places.\n\nWait, let me re-read: \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" - this is ambiguous about how many decimal places. I'll use round to 4 decimal places as a reasonable choice.\n\nNow the output contract: the response must be a single JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing Python source as a string.\n\nLet me write the Python implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    if threshold is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing threshold\")\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be a list\")\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be at least 1 for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = round(gain / prediction_tokens, 4)\n        \n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Now I need to format the entire response as a single JSON object with `\"implementation\"` key containing the Python source as a properly escaped JSON string.\n\nLet me write the final response carefully.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    if threshold is None:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing threshold\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        if not isinstance(prediction_tokens, (int, float)) or prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"prediction_tokens must be at least 1 for call {call_id}\\\")\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = round(gain / prediction_tokens, 4)\\n\\n        accepted = bool(parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01xUOvBwODh1St6r6idmSYe0","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2434},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2434,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":78,"output_tokens":1433,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1085},"service_tier":"standard"}}